<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Storting</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1814</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Stortinget</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Storting is the parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, established by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eidsvoll">Eidsvoll</a> Constitution of 17 May 1814. In November 1814 it accepted the union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xiii-of-sweden">Charles XIII of Sweden</a> as King of Norway while keeping the constitution. In 1905 it declared the union with Sweden dissolved. It is a unicameral assembly that meets in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/storting.jpg" alt="Storting" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GlowstoneUnknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2025_Norwegian_Storting.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
